IMPORT prelude

-- Factors Act 1889 (Singapore) -- when a person who is not the owner can nevertheless pass good title to goods: dispositions by a
-- mercantile agent (ss 1, 2, 6), pledges of documents and the limits on what a pledgee takes (ss 3, 4, 5), the consignee's lien (s 7),
-- the seller left in possession and the buyer let into possession (ss 8, 9), transfers that defeat a vendor's lien (s 10), how a
-- document is transferred (s 11), and what the true owner keeps (s 12).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FA1889.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; no later amendment
-- is annotated in the text. The deposit's metadata records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0036 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to the operative sections 1 to 12, which is nearly the whole Act (it has 14 sections). Not encoded:
-- s 13 (construction "in amplification and not in derogation" of an agent's common-law powers -- nothing to compute), s 14 (short
-- title), the meaning of "ordinary course of business", "good faith" and "notice" (taken as given facts), the civil and criminal
-- liability s 12(1) preserves (only that it survives is encoded), and the Sale of Goods Act provisions this Act sits beside.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Factors Act 1889 -- dispositions`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below zero` MEANS IF `x` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `x`

§§ `1, 2, 6 -- dispositions by a mercantile agent`

-- s 1(1): "mercantile agent" means one "having in the customary course of his business as such agent authority either to sell goods,
-- or to consign goods for the purpose of sale, or to buy goods, or to raise money on the security of goods".
-- s 1(2): a person is "deemed to be in possession" where the goods or documents "are in the person's actual custody or are held by any
-- other person subject to his control or for him or on his behalf".
-- s 6: an agreement made "through a clerk or other person authorised in the ordinary course of business to make contracts of sale or
-- pledge on his behalf shall be deemed to be an agreement with the agent".
DECLARE Disposition HAS
    `the agent is a mercantile agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made by the agent or an authorised clerk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agent had actual custody` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another held the goods for the agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is evidence the owner did not consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the documents came from consented possession` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the owner's consent had ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the ordinary course of business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taker acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taker had notice of no authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the taker had notice consent had ended` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `d` IS A Disposition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agent is in possession` IF
    `d`'s `the agent had actual custody` OR `d`'s `another held the goods for the agent`

-- s 2(3): where the agent obtained documents of title "by reason of his being or having been, with the consent of the owner, in
-- possession of the goods ... his possession of the first-mentioned documents shall ... be deemed to be with the consent of the owner".
-- s 2(4): "the consent of the owner shall be presumed in the absence of evidence to the contrary".
GIVEN `d` IS A Disposition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner consented to the agent's possession` IF
    `d`'s `the documents came from consented possession` OR (NOT `d`'s `there is evidence the owner did not consent`)

-- s 2(1): where a mercantile agent is, with the consent of the owner, in possession of goods or documents of title, "any sale, pledge,
-- or other disposition of the goods, made by him when acting in the ordinary course of business of a mercantile agent, shall ... be as
-- valid as if he were expressly authorised by the owner": "Provided that the person taking under the disposition acts in good faith,
-- and has not at the time of the disposition notice that the person making the disposition has no authority to make the same."
-- s 2(2): a disposition "which would have been valid if the consent had continued, shall be valid notwithstanding the determination
-- of the consent: Provided that the person taking under the disposition has not at the time thereof notice that the consent has been
-- determined."
GIVEN `d` IS A Disposition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disposition binds the owner` IF
        `d`'s `the agent is a mercantile agent`
    AND `d`'s `made by the agent or an authorised clerk`
    AND `the agent is in possession` `d`
    AND `the owner consented to the agent's possession` `d`
    AND `d`'s `in the ordinary course of business`
    AND `d`'s `the taker acted in good faith`
    AND (NOT `d`'s `the taker had notice of no authority`)
    AND (    (NOT `d`'s `the owner's consent had ended`)
          OR (NOT `d`'s `the taker had notice consent had ended`))

§§ `3, 4, 5 -- pledges`

-- s 3: "A pledge of the documents of title to goods shall be deemed to be a pledge of the goods."
GIVEN `pledged the documents of title` IS A BOOLEAN, `pledged the goods themselves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are pledged` IF `pledged the documents of title` OR `pledged the goods themselves`

-- s 4: where an agent pledges goods "as security for a debt or liability due from the pledgor to the pledgee before the time of the
-- pledge, the pledgee shall acquire no further right to the goods than could have been enforced by the pledgor at the time of the
-- pledge".
-- s 5: consideration may be cash, other goods, a document of title, a negotiable security "or any other valuable consideration"; "but
-- where goods are pledged by a mercantile agent in consideration of the delivery or transfer of other goods, or of a document of title
-- to goods, or of a negotiable security, the pledgee shall acquire no right or interest in the goods so pledged in excess of the value
-- of the goods, documents, or security when so delivered or transferred in exchange".
-- For a fresh cash advance the Act sets no cap of its own; returning the amount advanced is an INFERENCE that the pledge, being valid
-- under s 2, secures what was advanced.
DECLARE Consideration IS ONE OF
    `a fresh cash advance`
    `goods, documents or a negotiable security given in exchange`
    `a debt already owed by the agent`

GIVEN `what was given` IS A Consideration, `amount advanced or owed` IS A NUMBER, `value of what was exchanged` IS A NUMBER, `what the agent could enforce` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the pledgee can claim on the goods` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what was given`
    WHEN `a fresh cash advance` THEN `amount advanced or owed`
    WHEN `goods, documents or a negotiable security given in exchange` THEN `the lesser of` `amount advanced or owed` `value of what was exchanged`
    WHEN `a debt already owed by the agent` THEN `the lesser of` `amount advanced or owed` `what the agent could enforce`

§§ `7 -- consignees`

-- s 7(1): where the owner "has given possession of the goods to another person for the purpose of consignment or sale, or has shipped
-- the goods in the name of another person, and the consignee of the goods has not had notice that such person is not the owner of the
-- goods, the consignee shall, in respect of advances made to or for the use of such person, have the same lien on the goods as if such
-- person were the owner of the goods, and may transfer any such lien to another person".
GIVEN `the owner gave possession for consignment or sale, or shipped in another's name` IS A BOOLEAN, `the consignee had notice the consignor was not the owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `the consignee made advances to the consignor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consignee has a lien against the owner` IF
        `the owner gave possession for consignment or sale, or shipped in another's name`
    AND (NOT `the consignee had notice the consignor was not the owner`)
    AND `the consignee made advances to the consignor`

§§ `8, 9 -- sellers and buyers left in possession`

DECLARE Resale HAS
    `the seller stayed in possession after selling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the buyer got possession with the seller's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the goods or documents were delivered or transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the second taker acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the second taker had notice of the first sale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the second taker had notice of the seller's lien or right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the ordinary course of business` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 8: where a person, having sold goods, continues in possession of the goods or documents, "the delivery or transfer by that person
-- ... under any sale, pledge, or other disposition thereof, or under any agreement for sale ... to any person receiving the same in
-- good faith and without notice of the previous sale, shall have the same effect as if the person making the delivery or transfer
-- were expressly authorised by the owner".
GIVEN `r` IS A Resale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seller's second disposition binds the first buyer` IF
        `r`'s `the seller stayed in possession after selling`
    AND `r`'s `the goods or documents were delivered or transferred`
    AND `r`'s `the second taker acted in good faith`
    AND (NOT `r`'s `the second taker had notice of the first sale`)

-- s 9: where a person, "having bought or agreed to buy goods, obtains with the consent of the seller possession of the goods or the
-- documents", delivery or transfer by him "to any person receiving the same in good faith and without notice of any lien or other
-- right of the original seller ... shall have the same effect as if the person making the delivery or transfer were a mercantile agent
-- in possession of the goods or documents of title with the consent of the owner".
-- "The same effect as if ... a mercantile agent" sends the reader back to s 2(1), whose effect requires the agent to act "in the
-- ordinary course of business of a mercantile agent". Carrying that condition into s 9 is an INFERENCE from the words; s 9 does not
-- state it.
GIVEN `r` IS A Resale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the buyer's disposition defeats the original seller` IF
        `r`'s `the buyer got possession with the seller's consent`
    AND `r`'s `the goods or documents were delivered or transferred`
    AND `r`'s `the second taker acted in good faith`
    AND (NOT `r`'s `the second taker had notice of the seller's lien or right`)
    AND `r`'s `in the ordinary course of business`

§§ `10, 11 -- transfer of documents of title`

-- s 10: where a document of title "has been lawfully transferred to a person as a buyer or owner of the goods, and that person
-- transfers the document to a person who takes the document in good faith and for valuable consideration, the last-mentioned transfer
-- shall have the same effect for defeating any vendor's lien or right of stoppage in transitu as the transfer of a bill of lading".
GIVEN `the document was lawfully transferred to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the buyer transferred it on` IS A BOOLEAN, `the transferee took in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `the transferee gave valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vendor's lien or stoppage is defeated` IF
        `the document was lawfully transferred to the buyer`
    AND `the buyer transferred it on`
    AND `the transferee took in good faith`
    AND `the transferee gave valuable consideration`

-- s 11: "the transfer of a document may be by endorsement, or, where the document is by custom or by its express terms transferable by
-- delivery or makes the goods deliverable to the bearer, then by delivery".
DECLARE Method IS ONE OF `by endorsement`, `by delivery alone`

GIVEN `how` IS A Method, `transferable by delivery by custom or its terms` IS A BOOLEAN, `deliverable to bearer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document is transferred` IF
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `by endorsement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `by delivery alone` THEN `transferable by delivery by custom or its terms` OR `deliverable to bearer`

§§ `12 -- what the true owner keeps`

-- s 12(1): nothing in the Act authorises an agent "to exceed or depart from his authority as between himself and his principal, or
-- exempt him from any liability, civil or criminal, for so doing". So the agent's exposure does not depend on whether the disposition
-- binds the owner.
GIVEN `the agent exceeded his authority` IS A BOOLEAN, `the disposition bound the owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agent remains answerable to the owner` IF `the agent exceeded his authority`

-- s 12(2): nothing prevents the owner "from recovering the goods from any agent or his trustee in bankruptcy at any time before the
-- sale or pledge thereof".
GIVEN `the agent has sold the goods` IS A BOOLEAN, `the agent has pledged the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may take the goods back from the agent` IF
    (NOT `the agent has sold the goods`) AND (NOT `the agent has pledged the goods`)

-- s 12(2): the owner of goods pledged by an agent may "redeem the goods at any time before the sale thereof, on satisfying the claim for
-- which the goods were pledged, and paying to the agent, if by him required, any money in respect of which the agent would by law be
-- entitled to retain the goods ... by way of lien as against the owner".
GIVEN `the pledgee's claim` IS A NUMBER, `the agent's lien` IS A NUMBER, `the agent requires payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cost of redeeming the goods` MEANS
    IF `the agent requires payment` THEN `the pledgee's claim` PLUS `the agent's lien` ELSE `the pledgee's claim`

-- s 12(2): or "from recovering from any person with whom the goods have been pledged any balance of money remaining in his hands as the
-- produce of the sale of the goods after deducting the amount of his lien". Flooring at zero is an INFERENCE (a "balance" cannot be
-- negative).
GIVEN `the sale produced` IS A NUMBER, `the pledgee's lien` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the surplus the owner may recover from the pledgee` MEANS `not below zero` (`the sale produced` MINUS `the pledgee's lien`)

-- s 12(3): nothing prevents the owner of goods sold by an agent "from recovering from the buyer the price agreed to be paid for the same,
-- or any part of that price, subject to any right of set off on the part of the buyer against the agent". Flooring at zero is an
-- INFERENCE.
GIVEN `the unpaid price` IS A NUMBER, `the buyer's set-off against the agent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the price the owner may recover from the buyer` MEANS `not below zero` (`the unpaid price` MINUS `the buyer's set-off against the agent`)
